  "=segments": [
    {
      "line": 1,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Once upon a time, big stone people (Giants) and sky people (Nephoretti) became friends after being scared of each other."
    },
    {
      "line": 2,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They built towers that sang when the wind blew, and pointy mountains that helped plants grow."
    },
    {
      "line": 3,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Sometimes things fell down, but they kept trying for hundreds of years."
    },
    {
      "line": 4,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They made special places where magic felt strongest - like secret clubhouses for the whole world."
    },
    {
      "line": 5,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The stone people lived where they were happiest: some by water, some in forests, some underground."
    },
    {
      "line": 6,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The sky people visited everyone, helping them build better."
    },
    {
      "line": 7,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "They had big parties with music made from mountains and wind."
    },
    {
      "line": 8,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "But one day, darkness came from the sky like a bad storm that wouldn't stop."
    },
    {
      "line": 9,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "Strange ships arrived, and the friends knew their happy world was about to change forever."
    },
    {
      "line": 11,
      "type": "narration",
      "text": "The end (for now)."
    }
  ],
